From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matteo Pacini <m@matteopacini.me>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:42:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] mods: load mods from folders in HERDR_APP_MODS_PATH

herdr-app only loads mods from ~/.config/herdr-app/mods (plus its own frame
mods). This adds HERDR_APP_MODS_PATH, a PATH-style list of extra folders whose
subfolders with a main.js load as mods too, so a repo can ship a panel without
symlinking it into the home. On a name clash mods/ wins, then frame mods, then
the extra folders in order. The startup layout check and the key cleanup now
look in the extra folders too, so a layout or binding naming such a mod is kept.

Mods are trusted code with unrestricted exec and network access. Every folder
listed here runs automatically, so a git pull in a listed repo changes code
running with your environment. List only folders you trust.
